@Lauri  you wrote this in `src/hal/mux.cpp`; does this mean it's currently suffering the slow behavior but could do the fast if one edits in a mythical (doesn't seem particularly specified here, but I'd guess it's imported/included from platformio?) header file?

Because looking at the timing diagram in the datasheet we could let the falling clock coincide with the data transition.

I know you don't need it to be very fast, due to your fairly high-Z measurements, but for the FlexMem testing I'd like to be at least somewhat near the MUX chip's potential speed.

```
// Speed note: replace digitalWrite with gpio_set_mask/gpio_clr_mask (hardware/gpio.h)
// for ~50x speedup (~200 ns/transaction vs ~10 µs). All CH446X setup/hold
// requirements (3–10 ns) are met by back-to-back SIO writes without added delays.
```
